Yes — this is a very good use case for a **standardized application troubleshooting / deployment validation framework**.

The key idea I would recommend is: **don't make the checklist just a document that engineers read manually. Make it a decision tree that can eventually become an automated diagnostic workflow.**

## 1. Overall architecture

Your environment sounds roughly like:

                    Users / Devices
                          |
                          v
              Azure Application Gateway
                          |
                 Network / Ingress
                          |
                          v
                Kubernetes Cluster
                          |
              +-----------+-----------+
              |                       |
              v                       v
        Frontend / API          Other Services
              |
              v
          MongoDB
              
Monitoring:
  Application Logs
  Kubernetes Logs
  Application Gateway Logs
  MongoDB Metrics/Logs
  Network Tests
  CI/CD Pipeline
```

The troubleshooting process should sit **around this architecture**.

