# 3. Start with a "Golden Path"

Before troubleshooting an issue, define what a **healthy application** looks like.

For example:

### Application Golden Path

```text
Internet/User
    ↓
Azure Application Gateway
    ↓
Ingress
    ↓
Kubernetes Service
    ↓
Application Pod
    ↓
MongoDB
    ↓
Application Response
```

For every layer, define:

| Layer                  | Expected healthy state     |
| ---------------------- | -------------------------- |
| Application Gateway    | Healthy backend            |
| DNS                    | Resolves correctly         |
| TLS                    | Certificate valid          |
| Ingress                | Route exists               |
| Kubernetes             | Pods Running/Ready         |
| Service                | Endpoints available        |
| Application            | HTTP 200/expected response |
| MongoDB                | Reachable                  |
| MongoDB authentication | Successful                 |
| Application logs       | No critical errors         |
| CPU/Memory             | Within threshold           |
| Business login         | Test user can login        |
| Main functionality     | Test transaction succeeds  |

This becomes your **baseline**.

