# 6. Kubernetes diagnostic branch

When the process identifies Kubernetes as the possible problem, don't just say "check Kubernetes."

Break it down.

### Kubernetes checks

```text
Deployment
   |
   +--> Deployment exists?
   |
   +--> Desired replicas = actual replicas?
   |
   +--> Pods created?
   |
   +--> Pods Running?
   |
   +--> Pods Ready?
   |
   +--> Restart count?
   |
   +--> CrashLoopBackOff?
   |
   +--> ImagePullBackOff?
   |
   +--> OOMKilled?
   |
   +--> Readiness probe failing?
   |
   +--> Liveness probe failing?
   |
   +--> Events showing errors?
   |
   +--> Service endpoints present?
```

You can eventually automate most of these.

For example:

```text
kubectl get deployment
kubectl get pods
kubectl describe pod
kubectl get events
kubectl get svc
kubectl get endpoints
```

The checklist shouldn't necessarily expose commands to everyone. The eventual system can run them automatically.

