# 8. Application → MongoDB troubleshooting

This should be another independent branch.

```text
Application Pod
      |
      v
DNS resolution
      |
      v
MongoDB endpoint
      |
      v
Network connectivity
      |
      v
MongoDB port
      |
      v
Authentication
      |
      v
Database selection
      |
      v
Collection/query
```

Run checks in that order.

### MongoDB diagnostic tree

```text
Can application resolve MongoDB hostname?
          |
       NO → DNS issue
          |
         YES
          |
          v
Can application connect to MongoDB port?
          |
       NO → Network/firewall/security issue
          |
         YES
          |
          v
Can application authenticate?
          |
       NO → Credential/authentication issue
          |
         YES
          |
          v
Can application execute expected query?
          |
       NO → Database/application issue
          |
         YES
          |
          v
MongoDB healthy
```

This is much better than simply saying **"MongoDB is down."**

