# 16. I would structure the project into 5 layers

### Layer 1 — Architecture Blueprint

Document:

```text
Users
 ↓
Application Gateway
 ↓
Ingress
 ↓
Kubernetes
 ↓
Application
 ↓
MongoDB
```

And document every dependency.

---

### Layer 2 — Monitoring

Define what monitoring exists for each component:

```text
Application Gateway
Kubernetes
Application
MongoDB
Network
CI/CD
```

---

### Layer 3 — Diagnostic Checklist

Create checks:

```text
DNS
Network
Gateway
Kubernetes
Application
MongoDB
CI/CD
Business validation
```

---

### Layer 4 — Decision Engine

Define:

```text
IF check fails
THEN run these checks
ELSE move to next layer
```

This is the actual **troubleshooting intelligence**.

---

### Layer 5 — Automated Validation

Eventually integrate:

```text
CI/CD
  ↓
Deployment
  ↓
Automated Diagnostics
  ↓
Synthetic Test User
  ↓
Business Transaction
  ↓
PASS / FAIL
```

This means a deployment doesn't just finish when Kubernetes says:

> Deployment successful

Instead:

> **Deployment + infrastructure + application + database + business validation successful**

